{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"FOUR_TICKET_PROSE_AUDIT_FALLBACK_READBACK:d6669496\n\nAfter all target payloads were present, the mandated strict MCP readback was attempted serially. The first show_ticket (autositic-relaxative-nurseshark) returned no state and terminated at the 300s MCP client deadline, so the sequence stopped without launching the other three MCP reads. The sanctioned repo-venv fallback then projected and compared all four tickets: every description byte, ordered path/reason row, and normalized dd_id/dd_text/command triple matched; each ticket remained open, unassigned, parented to d6eb-1c6c-88c3-48f6, warning-free, and uncertified (the frozen CLI omits the modern attestations map, so this was checked as signature=null against the immediately preceding MCP preflight's attestations={}). The elder-stingy-narwhale receipt was pre-read at zero marker hits, appended once, and read back as one exact marker/body."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788639086360586001,"uuid":"8ce19fc0-5866-4d74-a596-01b63354e392"}